# The scene cases of fixtures/src/*.vexp that no toy EXPECT lists, one per line: CASE_ID, a TAB and the reason (plan 04-07; D-172, D-173, amendment A5). scripts/video-check reads this file; a line with no reason is VIDEO_EXEMPT_FORMAT, and the count of lines is printed in the VIDEO_CHECK status line.
# A scene case that a toy EXPECT lists with no second column needs no line here.
video_vce_pal_golden	golden change detector beside the literal case video_vce_pal, which vid-palette-mask kills
vid_frame_lines	the divider toy does not change line counts or the frame length: the scene is killed by the faults F4 and F9 of its sweep
video_bg_basic_golden	golden change detector beside the literal cases video_bg_basic_solid and video_bg_basic_asym, which vid-palette-mask and vid-bit-order kill
video_unmodelled_mode	a flag case: the toys leave the line records of the unmodelled frames alone, the scene is killed by the F0 of its fault sweep and by the negative row of frame 7
video_bg_scroll	the toy vid-scroll-latch follows in Task 3 of plan 04-12; until then the scene is killed by F0, F1, F7 and F8 of its fault sweep (added by Task 2)
video_bg_scroll_asym	killed by F0, F1, F7 and F8 of its fault sweep; the toy vid-scroll-latch moves only the BYR latch rows of video_bg_scroll, and the wrap and direction rows are ASSUMED readings that no mutant of the renderer is spent on (toy cap of 10)
video_bg_enab	killed by F0, F1, F7 and F3 of its fault sweep (the tile rows, the burst frame and the backdrop frame) and by F0 and F8 of the post-toggle rows; no toy of the renderer is spent on it (toy cap of 10)
